' ============================================================
' JSON - parse, inspect, edit and write JSON, in pure GBX
'
'@help
'# JSON
'
'Parse JSON into dictionaries, read and write values by path, build
'documents in code and serialize them back. Pure GBX: it runs in the
'interpreter, in a built EXE and in the HTML5 player.
'
'The module is the folder `modules/json`; `JSON.gbx` is its entry file.
'Add it with the Modules dock or write:
'
'```gbx
'INCLUDE "modules/json/JSON.gbx"
'```
'
'## Quick start
'
'```gbx
'INCLUDE "modules/json/JSON.gbx"
'
'doc = JSON_PARSE("{""player"":{""name"":""Ada"",""hp"":100},""tags"":[""rpg""]}")
'
'PRINT JSON_GET_TEXT$(doc, "player.name", "?"), 10, 10   ' Ada
'PRINT STR$(JSON_GET_NUM(doc, "player.hp", 0)), 10, 30  ' 100
'PRINT JSON_GET_TEXT$(doc, "tags[0]", "?"), 10, 50      ' rpg
'
'JSON_SET_NUM doc, "player.hp", 90
'JSON_APPEND_TEXT doc, "tags", "puzzle"
'PRINT JSON_WRITE$(doc), 10, 70
'```
'
'## Value model
'
'A parsed document uses the types GameBasiX already has:
'
'| JSON | GameBasiX |
'| --- | --- |
'| object | `DICT` with the marker key `"$"` = 10 |
'| array | `DICT` with the marker key `"$"` = 11 and the keys `"0"`, `"1"`, ... |
'| string | text |
'| number | number |
'| true / false | marked value, see `JSON_MAKE_TRUE()` / `JSON_MAKE_FALSE()` |
'| null | marked value, see `JSON_MAKE_NULL()` |
'
'Because objects and arrays are dictionaries, a document can be walked with
'`DICT_COUNT`, `DICT_KEY$` and `DICT_VALUE` as well - but skip the `"$"`
'marker. `JSON_KIND`, `JSON_READ_*` and the path functions take care of it.
'Object keys that start with `"$"` are escaped internally, so a real `"$"`
'key never collides with the marker.
'
'| Constant | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `JSON_TYPE_NULL` | 0 |
'| `JSON_TYPE_BOOL` | 1 |
'| `JSON_TYPE_NUMBER` | 2 |
'| `JSON_TYPE_STRING` | 3 |
'| `JSON_TYPE_OBJECT` | 4 |
'| `JSON_TYPE_ARRAY` | 5 |
'
'## Parsing and writing
'
'| Function | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `JSON_PARSE(text$)` | Parse a value; on error a null value is returned |
'| `JSON_VALID(text$)` | 1 when the text is valid JSON |
'| `JSON_ERROR$()` | Last parse error, with the character position |
'| `JSON_ERROR_POS()` | Position of the last error |
'| `JSON_READ(path$)` | Read a UTF-8 file and parse it |
'| `JSON_WRITE$(v)` | Compact JSON, one line |
'| `JSON_WRITE_PRETTY$(v)` | Indented with two spaces per level |
'| `JSON_WRITE_INDENTED$(v, indent)` | Indented with `indent` spaces |
'| `JSON_SAVE(v, path$)` | Write pretty JSON to a file, 1 on success |
'| `JSON_ESCAPE$(text$)` | Escape a string without the surrounding quotes |
'
'Parse errors never stop the program: `JSON_PARSE` returns a null value and
'`JSON_ERROR$()` explains what went wrong. Nesting is limited to 48 levels.
'
'## Reading by path
'
'| Function | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `JSON_GET(doc, path$)` | Raw value at the path, `0` when missing |
'| `JSON_HAS(doc, path$)` | 1 when the path exists (also for null values) |
'| `JSON_GET_TYPE(doc, path$)` | `JSON_TYPE_*`, `-1` when missing |
'| `JSON_GET_NUM(doc, path$, fallback)` | Number, boolean as 0/1, else fallback |
'| `JSON_GET_TEXT$(doc, path$, fallback$)` | Text, else fallback |
'| `JSON_GET_BOOL(doc, path$, fallback)` | Boolean, numbers as 1/0, else fallback |
'| `JSON_COUNT(doc, path$)` | Array length, object key count or text length |
'| `JSON_KEY$(doc, path$, index)` | Object key by position (insertion order) |
'| `JSON_AT(doc, path$, index)` | Array element or object value by position |
'
'A path is text: names select object keys, `[n]` selects an array element.
'
'```text
'player.name          object key inside "player"
'inventory[2].count   third element of the "inventory" array
'[0].id               first element of an array document
''                   the document itself
'```
'
'## Building and editing
'
'| Function | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `JSON_OBJECT()` | New empty object |
'| `JSON_ARRAY()` | New empty array |
'| `JSON_MAKE_NULL()`, `JSON_MAKE_TRUE()`, `JSON_MAKE_FALSE()`, `JSON_MAKE_BOOL(flag)` | Marked values |
'| `JSON_SET(doc, path$, v)` | Store a value, creating missing containers |
'| `JSON_SET_NULL`, `JSON_SET_BOOL`, `JSON_SET_NUM`, `JSON_SET_TEXT` | Typed variants |
'| `JSON_APPEND(doc, path$, v)` | Append to an array, returns the index or -1 |
'| `JSON_APPEND_NULL`, `JSON_APPEND_BOOL`, `JSON_APPEND_NUM`, `JSON_APPEND_TEXT` | Typed variants |
'| `JSON_REMOVE(doc, path$)` | Remove a key or element; arrays close the gap |
'| `JSON_CLEAR(doc, path$)` | Empty an object or array in place |
'| `JSON_CLONE(v)` | Deep copy of a value |
'
'`JSON_SET` creates objects and arrays along the path: setting
'`"world.rooms[3].name"` on a fresh object creates `world`, `rooms` and
'fills indices 0 to 2 with null. Setting a value that contradicts the path
'replaces the container, so `JSON_SET doc, "a.b", 1` after `a` was an array
'turns `a` into an object and vice versa.
'
'## Inspecting a value
'
'| Function | Meaning |
'| --- | --- |
'| `JSON_KIND(v)` | `JSON_TYPE_*` of any value |
'| `JSON_TYPE_NAME$(v)` | `"null"`, `"boolean"`, `"number"`, `"string"`, `"object"`, `"array"` |
'| `JSON_IS_NULL`, `JSON_IS_BOOL`, `JSON_IS_NUMBER`, `JSON_IS_STRING`, `JSON_IS_OBJECT`, `JSON_IS_ARRAY` | Type tests |
'| `JSON_BOOL(v)` | true as 1, everything else 0 |
'| `JSON_NUM(v)` | Number value, 0 otherwise |
'| `JSON_TEXT$(v)` | Text value, "" otherwise |
'
'Native GBX arrays can be serialized as JSON arrays, and `JSON_AT` reads
'them; parsed documents always use the dictionary representation so they can
'mix numbers, text, objects and arrays freely.
'
'@endhelp

INCLUDE "value.gbx"
INCLUDE "path.gbx"
INCLUDE "parse.gbx"
INCLUDE "write.gbx"
